Carafe: fewer waits of the game thread for the front end. A managed buffer that no queued call has used and that was
never locked past the front end gets empty memory at its first lock, freed at the unlock, as its contents are not yet
defined; a game that creates buffers while it plays and fills each once no longer waits for every one of them.
The end of an event query is queued, and asking for its result no longer waits for the queue: until the queued end
has run the event is not signalled, as on a busy GPU, and a flush the game asks for is queued once per end.
SetGammaRamp with the ramp already set returns at once. DISCARD locks of up to 256 KB, not 64 KB, are staged. The
handle lookups of Wine's effect interface, which only read the effect's structure, are called without waiting. The
report counts the new buffers locked this way, the size of the buffer locks that wait and the waits of the effect
library's methods that are not queued.
Zlib, as the files it changes.

